The desk merged every date report into #4471 and marked it known, with one fix queued. The
reports hold two problems. This page splits them. The tickets are in the
[project issues](https://github.com/franProton100/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues).

<Callout kind="warn">
Counts are from the export of 4 October. The desk keeps working, so live numbers may differ.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemCounts ticket={4471} leftIn={['R-41202', 'R-41209', 'R-41236', 'R-41344', 'R-41620']} />

1. **Month and day swapped.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Tenants that write
   the day first get flipped dates. Ticket
   [#1](https://github.com/franProton100/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
2. **Form hint.** Day-first tenants on the booking-v3 form see an MM/DD hint, so people type month
   first. This needs a different fix from the parser. Ticket
   [#2](https://github.com/franProton100/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## How the reports were sorted

- One id is one report. The export overlaps, so repeats are removed first.
- A report's cause comes from its **tenant** (the locale it writes dates in, and its booking
  form), not from the subject line. The desk merged by subject, and that is how two problems
  became one ticket.
- The **intake tag** is a guess from the reporter's browser. It is shown for comparison and is
  never used to sort.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table's "no ticket of its own" note predates tickets 1 and 2 and is out of date.

## What we do not know

<Callout>
Five reports were flagged by the desk as a one-day move: R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and
R-41620. By tenant they belong to the shared parser, so they are counted there and footnoted. Some
describe a date one day off in the same month, which a plain day/month swap does not produce. A
separate cause could not be confirmed from five reports, so no separate ticket was kept. One
reporter says only June is affected; that is not checked against other reports. R-41236 describes
no day shift at all.
</Callout>

The form hint cause comes from tenant and form data. The reports' own text never mentions the form.

